Z||000007||Cooter||03-02-2000||04:35 PM||||Last summer, a friend and I were discussing the impending y2k bug and decided that motor fuel might get expensive if the bug really bit. So, we went to a local station with three 55 gallon drums and tanked up at .80 per gallon. I have not had to buy fuel from a station in a month! My wife made fun of us for buying and storing that much fuel, but I am the one laughing at her now.||||reg||1
